---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Prose from "../components/Prose.astro";
---
<Base
  title="Privacy · nyq"
  description="What the nyq website and the nyq command line tool send, and to whom."
  current="privacy"
>
  <Prose title="Privacy" updated="2 November 2026">
    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>
      This site is a set of static pages. It sets no cookies, runs no analytics and loads no third
      party scripts. The host serving the pages may keep standard request logs, such as your IP
      address and browser, under its own privacy policy.
    </p>
    <h2>The nyq tool</h2>
    <p>nyq has no telemetry and no account with us. It makes these network requests:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>To the model provider you choose, carrying your conversation, the files and command output the agent reads, and your credentials for that provider.</li>
      <li>To <code>models.dev</code>, at most once a day, for public model names, context sizes and prices.</li>
      <li>To GitHub, to look for and download new releases. Turn this off with <code>auto_upgrade = false</code> or <code>NYQ_AUTO_UPGRADE=0</code>.</li>
      <li>To web pages and search, only when the agent uses its web tools, and to MCP servers you configure.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      What your model provider does with your data is set by its own terms and privacy policy.
    </p>
    <h2>Data on your machine</h2>
    <p>
      Sign ins and API keys are stored under <code>~/.nyq</code> in files only your user can read.
      Conversations are saved as JSONL under <code>~/.nyq/sessions</code>. <code>nyq logout</code>{" "}
      removes stored sign ins, and <code>nyq session delete</code> removes a conversation.
    </p>
  </Prose>
</Base>
